IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT domain
IMPORT `g5-interpretation`
IMPORT `g5-nouns`

-- g5-art13-effects.l4: Article 13(1) to (5), (11) and (13) of the Charities (Jersey) Law 2014 -- what registration does to the entity's
-- constitution and what it requires of the registered charity.  Paragraphs (6) to (10) and (12) (the reports, the annual return and the
-- Orders) are in g5-art13-reporting.  The quotations are copied mechanically from the Law's text file by srcrefs.py; an `@ref` carries
-- the locator of the lines it rests on.
-- Reading guide.  A judgement of the Commissioner or the court ("to the satisfaction of", "inconsistent with") is a Boolean input named for what is judged.
-- Orders and Regulations are not in the sources, so what they prescribe is an input.  A duty, power or prohibition is a regulative rule;
-- where its precondition is a test over facts, the test is a BOOLEAN of its own, so a caller can ask the question without running a trace.
-- Forks: F5.6 (end of the registration), F5.7 (a purpose that is not charitable), F5.8 (paragraphs (a) and (b) of 13(5)); see g5-interpretation.

§ `Part 4 -- Charity register`

§§ `13 Effects of registration`

§§§ `13(1) The period during which paragraphs (2) to (4) apply`

-- Fork F5.6.  A registration that ends is ended on the day deregistration takes effect: for a deregistration with retrospective effect under
-- Article 17(3) that is the past date the Commissioner specified, "for all purposes", so a day between that past date and the notice is no longer
-- a day of registration (trap T15).  Whether the effective day itself is inside the registration is the fork.
-- Reading A (taken): the day deregistration takes effect is outside.
@ref Article 13(1) (src:372)
GIVEN effective IS A DATE
      `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`F5.6 A: the day is before the day deregistration takes effect` effective `the day` MEANS
    `the day` LESS THAN effective

-- Reading B: the day deregistration takes effect is still a day of registration.
@ref Article 13(1) (src:372)
GIVEN effective IS A DATE
      `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`F5.6 B: the day is not after the day deregistration takes effect` effective `the day` MEANS
    `the day` AT MOST effective

@ref Article 13(1) (src:372)
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 13 and 14`
      `the registered charity` IS A `Registered charity`
      `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 13(1) the registration has not ended on the day` interp `the registered charity` `the day` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the registered charity`'s `date deregistered`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
    WHEN JUST effective THEN
        CONSIDER interp's `whether the day deregistration takes effect is inside the registration`
        WHEN `outside: registered up to the day before deregistration takes effect`
            THEN `F5.6 A: the day is before the day deregistration takes effect` effective `the day`
        WHEN `inside: registered up to and including the day deregistration takes effect`
            THEN `F5.6 B: the day is not after the day deregistration takes effect` effective `the day`

-- src:372 | (1) Paragraphs (2) to (4) apply while an entity is registered as a charity, and only cease to apply if the entity is deregistered.
@ref Article 13(1) (src:372)
@export Whether paragraphs (2) to (4) of Article 13 apply to the entity on a day: from the day it was registered until deregistration takes effect (the reading of the day deregistration takes effect is a fork)
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 13 and 14` @desc The readings of the Law's open points; the default reading of each is TYPICALLY recorded in the record
      `the registered charity` IS A `Registered charity` @desc What the register holds about the charity, including the date it was registered and, if it has been deregistered, the day deregistration takes effect (the past date, for a deregistration with retrospective effect)
      `the day` IS A DATE @desc The day on which the question is asked
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 13(1) paragraphs (2) to (4) apply on the day` interp `the registered charity` `the day` MEANS
        `the day` AT LEAST `the registered charity`'s `date registered`
    AND `Art 13(1) the registration has not ended on the day` interp `the registered charity` `the day`

§§§ `13(2) A provision of the constitution that would let the purposes include a purpose that is not charitable`

-- The words of Article 6 and Article 5(1)(a)(ii) on which a purpose's charitableness turns are G2's; the Purpose record holds the result of
-- G2's classification (its head, and the flags for 6(5), 6(2)(f) and 5(1)(a)(ii)).  A purpose is charitable if it is not a political
-- purpose (6(5): neither charitable nor ancillary, whatever head it might fall under) and it falls under a head of 6(1) or is the advancement
-- of a philosophical belief (6(2)(f): analogous to the advancement of religion, so within 6(1)(p)).
@ref Article 13(2) (src:373)
GIVEN purpose IS A Purpose
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 13(2) the purpose is a charitable purpose` purpose MEANS
        NOT purpose's `is advancing a political party or promoting a candidate for election`
    AND (   isJust (purpose's head)
         OR purpose's `is advancing a philosophical belief`)

@ref Article 13(2) (src:373)
GIVEN purpose IS A Purpose
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 13(2) the purpose is purely ancillary or incidental to a charitable purpose` purpose MEANS
        NOT purpose's `is advancing a political party or promoting a candidate for election`
    AND purpose's `is purely ancillary or incidental to a charitable purpose of the entity`

-- Fork F5.7.  Reading A (taken, the literal one): "a purpose that is not charitable" is any purpose that is not a charitable purpose
-- under Article 6, so a purely ancillary purpose (Article 5(1)(a)(ii)) is caught.
@ref Article 13(2) (src:373)
GIVEN purpose IS A Purpose
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`F5.7 A: the purpose is not a charitable purpose under Article 6` purpose MEANS
    NOT `Art 13(2) the purpose is a charitable purpose` purpose

-- Reading B: only a purpose that is neither charitable nor purely ancillary or incidental is caught, which is what the charity test of
-- Article 5(1)(a) would reject.
@ref Article 13(2) (src:373)
GIVEN purpose IS A Purpose
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`F5.7 B: the purpose is neither charitable nor purely ancillary or incidental` purpose MEANS
        NOT `Art 13(2) the purpose is a charitable purpose` purpose
    AND NOT `Art 13(2) the purpose is purely ancillary or incidental to a charitable purpose` purpose

@ref Article 13(2) (src:373)
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 13 and 14`
      purpose IS A Purpose
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 13(2) the purpose is not charitable` interp purpose MEANS
    CONSIDER interp's `the meaning of a purpose that is not charitable`
    WHEN `any purpose that is not a charitable purpose under Article 6, a purely ancillary purpose included`
        THEN `F5.7 A: the purpose is not a charitable purpose under Article 6` purpose
    WHEN `a purpose that is neither a charitable purpose nor purely ancillary or incidental to one`
        THEN `F5.7 B: the purpose is neither charitable nor purely ancillary or incidental` purpose

@ref Article 13(2) (src:373)
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 13 and 14`
      provision IS A `Provision about amending purposes`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 13(2) the provision purports to permit a purpose that is not charitable` interp provision MEANS
        provision's `purports to permit an amendment to include any purpose whatever`
    OR  any (GIVEN purpose YIELD `Art 13(2) the purpose is not charitable` interp purpose)
            (provision's `purposes whose addition or substitution it purports to permit`)

-- src:373 | (2) Any provision of the entity’s constitution or constitutional Law is of no effect to the extent that it purports to permit an amendment of the purposes of the entity to include a purpose that is not charitable.
@ref Article 13(2) (src:373)
@export Whether a provision of a registered charity's constitution or constitutional Law is, on the day, of no effect under Article 13(2) because it purports to permit an amendment of the purposes to include a purpose that is not charitable
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 13 and 14` @desc The readings of the Law's open points; fork F5.7 decides whether a purely ancillary purpose is a purpose that is not charitable
      `the registered charity` IS A `Registered charity` @desc What the register holds about the charity
      `the day` IS A DATE @desc The day on which the question is asked
      provision IS A `Provision about amending purposes` @desc The provision of the constitution or constitutional Law and the purposes it purports to let an amendment add or substitute
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 13(2) the provision of the constitution is of no effect` interp `the registered charity` `the day` provision MEANS
        `Art 13(1) paragraphs (2) to (4) apply on the day` interp `the registered charity` `the day`
    AND provision's `forms part of the entity's constitution or constitutional Law`
    AND NOT `Art 13(13) paragraphs (2) and (3) yield to an order under the Loi of 1862` `the registered charity` provision
    AND `Art 13(2) the provision purports to permit a purpose that is not charitable` interp provision

§§§ `13(3) A provision that would let the purposes be amended to a different charitable purpose`

@ref Article 13(3) (src:374)
GIVEN provision IS A `Provision about amending purposes`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 13(3) the provision purports to permit a different charitable purpose to be added or substituted` provision MEANS
        provision's `purports to permit an amendment to include any purpose whatever`
    OR  any (GIVEN purpose YIELD `Art 13(2) the purpose is a charitable purpose` purpose)
            (provision's `purposes whose addition or substitution it purports to permit`)

-- src:374 | (3) Any provision of the entity’s constitution or constitutional Law that purports to permit an amendment of the purposes of the entity to add or substitute a different charitable purpose, is to be read as being subject to the entity –
@ref Article 13(3) (src:374)
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 13 and 14`
      `the registered charity` IS A `Registered charity`
      `the day` IS A DATE
      provision IS A `Provision about amending purposes`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 13(3) paragraph (3) applies to the provision` interp `the registered charity` `the day` provision MEANS
        `Art 13(1) paragraphs (2) to (4) apply on the day` interp `the registered charity` `the day`
    AND provision's `forms part of the entity's constitution or constitutional Law`
    AND NOT `Art 13(13) paragraphs (2) and (3) yield to an order under the Loi of 1862` `the registered charity` provision
    AND `Art 13(3) the provision purports to permit a different charitable purpose to be added or substituted` provision

-- The provision "is to be read as being subject to the entity" doing both (a) and (b).  The result is TRUE when paragraph (3) leaves the amendment
-- open: it does not apply, or it applies and the entity has both provided the evidence and obtained the prior approval.  "To the satisfaction of the
-- Commissioner" and "prior approval" are the Commissioner's: inputs.  The ordering "prior" is a fact a witness can state (the approval was
-- obtained before the amendment was made); the Law does not say how the same day is to be treated, and the dates are not modelled.
-- src:375 | (a) providing evidence, to the satisfaction of the Commissioner, of a reason justifying the proposed amendment; and
-- src:376 | (b) obtaining the Commissioner’s prior approval of the proposed amendment.
@ref Article 13(3)(a) and (b) (src:375-376)
@export Whether, on the day, Article 13(3) leaves open an amendment of a registered charity's purposes that a provision of its constitution purports to permit: TRUE if paragraph (3) does not apply, or the entity has provided evidence to the Commissioner's satisfaction of a reason justifying the amendment and obtained the Commissioner's prior approval
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 13 and 14` @desc The readings of the Law's open points
      `the registered charity` IS A `Registered charity` @desc What the register holds about the charity
      `the day` IS A DATE @desc The day on which the question is asked
      provision IS A `Provision about amending purposes` @desc The provision of the constitution or constitutional Law
      `evidence has been provided to the satisfaction of the Commissioner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Article 13(3)(a): the entity has provided evidence of a reason justifying the proposed amendment, and the Commissioner is satisfied with it
      `the Commissioner's approval was obtained before the amendment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Article 13(3)(b): the entity obtained the Commissioner's approval of the proposed amendment before the amendment was made
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 13(3) the amendment of purposes is subject to evidence and approval` interp `the registered charity` `the day` provision `evidence has been provided to the satisfaction of the Commissioner` `the Commissioner's approval was obtained before the amendment` MEANS
    IF `Art 13(3) paragraph (3) applies to the provision` interp `the registered charity` `the day` provision
    THEN "(a)" ... `evidence has been provided to the satisfaction of the Commissioner`
         AND "(b)" ... `the Commissioner's approval was obtained before the amendment`
    ELSE TRUE

-- Article 13 speaks of the Commissioner's approval and permission only from the side of the entity that must obtain it (13(3)(b), 13(4)(b),
-- 13(5)(b), 13(11)(b)); Article 33(2)(d) and (e) show that a refusal of approval under 13(3) and 13(4)(b) is a decision of the Commissioner.  Each is
-- encoded as the Commissioner's permission (MAY), implied by those words, and is marked as implied: the Law states no criteria and no time.
-- Whether the Commissioner approves is the Commissioner's discretion and is not computed; an unexercised permission is FULFILLED.
-- src:376 | (b) obtaining the Commissioner’s prior approval of the proposed amendment.
@ref Article 13(3)(b) (src:376) -- the Commissioner's power to approve is implied by these words
@export The Commissioner's permission (implied by Article 13(3)(b)) to approve a proposed amendment of a registered charity's purposes, as a regulative rule
GIVEN `someone is acting as the Commissioner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person appointed as the Commissioner, or a designated relevant person while the appointee cannot act, is acting
      `the entity has proposed an amendment of its purposes and asked for approval` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the registered charity has proposed an amendment of its purposes and asked the Commissioner to approve it
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Legal actor` `Act under Article 13`
`Art 13(3)(b) the Commissioner may approve the proposed amendment of purposes` `someone is acting as the Commissioner` `the entity has proposed an amendment of its purposes and asked for approval` MEANS
    IF     `someone is acting as the Commissioner`
       AND `the entity has proposed an amendment of its purposes and asked for approval`
    THEN PARTY `the Commissioner`
         MAY `give an approval or permission` `approval of a proposed amendment of the charity's purposes, Article 13(3)(b)`
         HENCE FULFILLED
    ELSE FULFILLED

§§§ `13(4) What the entity must do while it is registered`

-- (a) is a continuing duty with no time in the Law, so the rule carries no WITHIN; whether the charity in fact provides public benefit in
-- accordance with its registered public benefit statement is a judgement, so it is an input, and an act of providing it counts only if the input says so.
-- src:377 | (4) The entity must –
-- src:378 | (a) provide public benefit in accordance with its registered public benefit statement; and
@ref Article 13(4)(a) (src:377-378)
@export The duty of a registered charity to provide public benefit in accordance with its registered public benefit statement, as a regulative rule that applies on the days Article 13(1) says paragraphs (2) to (4) apply
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 13 and 14` @desc The readings of the Law's open points
      `the registered charity` IS A `Registered charity` @desc What the register holds about the charity, including its registered public benefit statement
      `the day` IS A DATE @desc The day on which the question is asked
      `public benefit is provided in accordance with the registered public benefit statement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc The judgement that the charity provides public benefit in accordance with its registered public benefit statement
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Legal actor` `Act under Article 13`
`Art 13(4) the registered charity must provide public benefit in accordance with its statement` interp `the registered charity` `the day` `public benefit is provided in accordance with the registered public benefit statement` MEANS
    IF `Art 13(1) paragraphs (2) to (4) apply on the day` interp `the registered charity` `the day`
    THEN PARTY `a registered charity`
         MUST `provide public benefit in accordance with the registered public benefit statement` (`the registered charity`'s `registered public benefit statement`)
              PROVIDED `public benefit is provided in accordance with the registered public benefit statement`
         HENCE FULFILLED
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- (b): the evidence is "to the satisfaction of the Commissioner", an input; evidence that does not satisfy the Commissioner is not performance.
-- src:379 | (b) if it requests the Commissioner’s approval of a proposed amendment to that statement, provide evidence, to the satisfaction of the Commissioner, of a reason justifying that request.
@ref Article 13(4)(b) (src:379)
@export The duty of a registered charity that requests the Commissioner's approval of a proposed amendment of its registered public benefit statement to provide evidence, to the Commissioner's satisfaction, of a reason justifying the request, as a regulative rule that applies on the days Article 13(1) says paragraphs (2) to (4) apply
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 13 and 14` @desc The readings of the Law's open points
      `the registered charity` IS A `Registered charity` @desc What the register holds about the charity
      `the day` IS A DATE @desc The day on which the question is asked
      `the entity requests the Commissioner's approval of a proposed amendment of its registered public benefit statement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the charity has asked the Commissioner to approve a proposed amendment of its registered public benefit statement
      `the evidence is to the satisfaction of the Commissioner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the evidence the charity gave of a reason justifying the request satisfies the Commissioner
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Legal actor` `Act under Article 13`
`Art 13(4)(b) the registered charity that requests approval of an amendment of its statement must provide evidence` interp `the registered charity` `the day` `the entity requests the Commissioner's approval of a proposed amendment of its registered public benefit statement` `the evidence is to the satisfaction of the Commissioner` MEANS
    IF     `Art 13(1) paragraphs (2) to (4) apply on the day` interp `the registered charity` `the day`
       AND `the entity requests the Commissioner's approval of a proposed amendment of its registered public benefit statement`
    THEN PARTY `a registered charity`
         MUST `provide evidence of a reason justifying the request, to the satisfaction of the Commissioner`
              PROVIDED `the evidence is to the satisfaction of the Commissioner`
         HENCE FULFILLED
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- src:379 | (b) if it requests the Commissioner’s approval of a proposed amendment to that statement, provide evidence, to the satisfaction of the Commissioner, of a reason justifying that request.
@ref Article 13(4)(b) (src:379) -- the Commissioner's power to approve is implied by these words
@export The Commissioner's permission (implied by Article 13(4)(b)) to approve a proposed amendment of a registered charity's registered public benefit statement, as a regulative rule
GIVEN `someone is acting as the Commissioner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person appointed as the Commissioner, or a designated relevant person while the appointee cannot act, is acting
      `the entity has requested approval of a proposed amendment of its registered public benefit statement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the registered charity has asked the Commissioner to approve the amendment
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Legal actor` `Act under Article 13`
`Art 13(4)(b) the Commissioner may approve the proposed amendment of the statement` `someone is acting as the Commissioner` `the entity has requested approval of a proposed amendment of its registered public benefit statement` MEANS
    IF     `someone is acting as the Commissioner`
       AND `the entity has requested approval of a proposed amendment of its registered public benefit statement`
    THEN PARTY `the Commissioner`
         MAY `give an approval or permission` `approval of a proposed amendment of the registered public benefit statement, Article 13(4)(b)`
         HENCE FULFILLED
    ELSE FULFILLED

§§§ `13(5) The condition of the restricted section`

-- Fork F5.8.  Paragraph (5) says "ensure (a) that it meets the condition ...; or (b) if, before it ceased to meet that condition, the Commissioner
-- gave prior permission ..., that it meets that condition as specified in that permission".
-- Reading A (taken): either.  (b) is open only to a charity that has ceased to meet the original condition and whose permission was given before it ceased.
@ref Article 13(5) (src:380-382)
GIVEN facts IS A `Facts about the condition of the restricted section`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`F5.8 A: either the original condition, or after a prior permission and a cessation the different condition` facts MEANS
        "(a)" ... facts's `meets the condition as to which the Commissioner was satisfied under Article 9(6)(b)`
    OR  (    "(b)" ... facts's `the Commissioner gave permission to remain entered on the basis of a different condition`
         AND facts's `that permission was given before the charity ceased to meet the original condition`
         AND facts's `ceased to meet that condition`
         AND facts's `meets the different condition as specified in the permission`)

-- Reading B: a prior permission replaces the original condition once given; the charity then has to meet the different condition whether or not it has
-- ceased to meet the original.
@ref Article 13(5) (src:380-382)
GIVEN facts IS A `Facts about the condition of the restricted section`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`F5.8 B: once a prior permission is given the different condition replaces the original condition` facts MEANS
    IF     facts's `the Commissioner gave permission to remain entered on the basis of a different condition`
       AND facts's `that permission was given before the charity ceased to meet the original condition`
    THEN facts's `meets the different condition as specified in the permission`
    ELSE facts's `meets the condition as to which the Commissioner was satisfied under Article 9(6)(b)`

-- src:380 | (5) A registered charity must, while it is entered in the restricted section of the register, ensure –
-- src:381 | (a) that it meets the condition, prescribed under Article 9(2), as to which the Commissioner was satisfied under Article 9(6)(b); or
-- src:382 | (b) if, before it ceased to meet that condition, the Commissioner gave prior permission for it to remain entered in the restricted section on the basis of a different condition prescribed under that Article, that it meets that condition as specified in that permission.
@ref Article 13(5)(a) and (b) (src:380-382)
@export Whether a registered charity entered in the restricted section meets what Article 13(5) requires of it: the condition on which the Commissioner was satisfied under Article 9(6)(b), or, after a prior permission given before it ceased to meet that condition, the different condition the permission specifies (the combination of the two paragraphs is a fork)
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 13 and 14` @desc The readings of the Law's open points; fork F5.8 decides how paragraphs (a) and (b) combine
      facts IS A `Facts about the condition of the restricted section` @desc Whether the charity meets the condition it was entered on, whether it has ceased to meet it, and the facts about any permission to remain on a different condition
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 13(5) the registered charity in the restricted section meets what paragraph (5) requires` interp facts MEANS
    CONSIDER interp's `how the two paragraphs of Article 13(5) combine`
    WHEN `either the original condition, or after a prior permission and a cessation the different condition`
        THEN `F5.8 A: either the original condition, or after a prior permission and a cessation the different condition` facts
    WHEN `once permission is given the different condition replaces the original condition`
        THEN `F5.8 B: once a prior permission is given the different condition replaces the original condition` facts

-- The duty arises "while it is entered in the restricted section of the register" and has no time.  Like 13(4)(a) it is a standing duty; an act of
-- ensuring counts only if the condition is in fact met.
-- src:380 | (5) A registered charity must, while it is entered in the restricted section of the register, ensure –
@ref Article 13(5) (src:380)
@export The duty of a registered charity, while it is entered in the restricted section of the register, to ensure that it meets the condition on which it is entered (or the different condition a prior permission specifies), as a regulative rule
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 13 and 14` @desc The readings of the Law's open points
      `the entity is a registered charity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the entity is entered for the time being in the general or the restricted section of the register
      `the registered charity` IS A `Registered charity` @desc What the register holds about the charity, including the section it is entered in
      facts IS A `Facts about the condition of the restricted section` @desc The facts about the condition and any permission
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Legal actor` `Act under Article 13`
`Art 13(5) the registered charity in the restricted section must ensure it meets its condition` interp `the entity is a registered charity` `the registered charity` facts MEANS
    IF     `the entity is a registered charity`
       AND `the registered charity`'s entity's `standing on the register` EQUALS `entered in the restricted section`
    THEN PARTY `a registered charity`
         MUST `ensure that the charity meets the condition on which it is entered in the restricted section`
              PROVIDED `Art 13(5) the registered charity in the restricted section meets what paragraph (5) requires` interp facts
         HENCE FULFILLED
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- src:382 | (b) if, before it ceased to meet that condition, the Commissioner gave prior permission for it to remain entered in the restricted section on the basis of a different condition prescribed under that Article, that it meets that condition as specified in that permission.
@ref Article 13(5)(b) (src:382) -- the Commissioner's power to give prior permission is presupposed by these words and conferred by no provision
@export The Commissioner's permission (presupposed by Article 13(5)(b); no provision confers it in terms) to give a registered charity prior permission to remain entered in the restricted section on the basis of a different condition, as a regulative rule
GIVEN `someone is acting as the Commissioner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person appointed as the Commissioner, or a designated relevant person while the appointee cannot act, is acting
      `the charity is entered in the restricted section` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the registered charity is entered in the restricted section of the register
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Legal actor` `Act under Article 13`
`Art 13(5)(b) the Commissioner may give prior permission to remain in the restricted section` `someone is acting as the Commissioner` `the charity is entered in the restricted section` MEANS
    IF     `someone is acting as the Commissioner`
       AND `the charity is entered in the restricted section`
    THEN PARTY `the Commissioner`
         MAY `give an approval or permission` `prior permission to remain entered in the restricted section on the basis of a different condition, Article 13(5)(b)`
         HENCE FULFILLED
    ELSE FULFILLED

§§§ `13(11) Payments inconsistent with the statement of intentions; permission to amend the statement`

-- The statement is the one a registered charity provides under an Order under 13(9)(b), a statement of its "current intentions".  Whether a payment
-- is "inconsistent with" a statement is a judgement (an input, asked of each statement provided).  Fork F5.14: which statement a payment is judged
-- by when the charity has provided several over time (permission to amend "that statement" is 13(11)(b)).  The prohibition has no time and the Law
-- attaches no penalty to it (it creates no offence); a contravention is misconduct under Article 2(10)(a)(i) (integration point IP13).
@ref Article 13(11)(a) (src:401-402)
GIVEN payment IS A `Payment by the charity`
GIVETH A LIST OF `Statement of intentions as to payments`
`Art 13(11)(a) the statements provided on or before the day of the payment` payment MEANS
    filter (GIVEN statement YIELD statement's `date provided` AT MOST payment's `date of the payment`)
           (payment's `statements provided`)

-- Reading A (taken): the statement in force on the day of the payment, the latest provided on or before that day, the earlier ones having been amended.
@ref Article 13(11)(a) (src:401-402)
GIVEN payment IS A `Payment by the charity`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`F5.14 A: the payment is inconsistent with the statement in force on the day of the payment` payment MEANS
    IF null eligible
    THEN FALSE
    ELSE any (GIVEN statement YIELD     Day (statement's `date provided`) EQUALS latest
                                    AND statement's `the payment is inconsistent with it`)
             eligible
    WHERE
        eligible MEANS `Art 13(11)(a) the statements provided on or before the day of the payment` payment
        latest MEANS maximum (map (GIVEN statement YIELD Day (statement's `date provided`)) eligible)

-- Reading B: "a statement provided under paragraph (9)(b)" is any statement provided on or before the day of the payment.
@ref Article 13(11)(a) (src:401-402)
GIVEN payment IS A `Payment by the charity`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`F5.14 B: the payment is inconsistent with any statement provided on or before the day of the payment` payment MEANS
    any (GIVEN statement YIELD statement's `the payment is inconsistent with it`)
        (`Art 13(11)(a) the statements provided on or before the day of the payment` payment)

@ref Article 13(11)(a) (src:401-402)
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 13 and 14`
      payment IS A `Payment by the charity`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 13(11)(a) the payment is inconsistent with the statement` interp payment MEANS
    CONSIDER interp's `the statement a payment must be consistent with`
    WHEN `the statement in force on the day of the payment`
        THEN `F5.14 A: the payment is inconsistent with the statement in force on the day of the payment` payment
    WHEN `any statement provided on or before the day of the payment`
        THEN `F5.14 B: the payment is inconsistent with any statement provided on or before the day of the payment` payment

-- src:401 | (11) A registered charity –
-- src:402 | (a) must not make any payment that is inconsistent with a statement provided under paragraph (9)(b);
@ref Article 13(11)(a) (src:401-402)
@export The prohibition on a registered charity making a payment that is inconsistent with the statement of its current intentions provided under an Order under Article 13(9)(b), as a regulative rule: it applies only if an Order under Article 13(9) applies to the charity; a payment is judged by the statement in force on its day (or by any statement provided, as the reading says); a payment made when no statement had been provided is not inconsistent with one
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 13 and 14` @desc The readings of the Law's open points; fork F5.14 decides which statement a payment is judged by
      `the entity is a registered charity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the entity is entered for the time being in the general or the restricted section of the register
      `an Order under Article 13(9) applies to the registered charity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether an Order under Article 13(9) applies to the registered charity (not relieved by an Order under Article 13(10))
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Legal actor` `Act under Article 13`
`Art 13(11)(a) the registered charity must not make a payment inconsistent with its statement` interp `the entity is a registered charity` `an Order under Article 13(9) applies to the registered charity` MEANS
    IF     `the entity is a registered charity`
       AND `an Order under Article 13(9) applies to the registered charity`
    THEN PARTY `a registered charity`
         SHANT `make a payment` payment
               PROVIDED `Art 13(11)(a) the payment is inconsistent with the statement` interp payment
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY `a registered charity` BECAUSE "Article 13(11)(a): the charity made a payment inconsistent with the statement provided under Article 13(9)(b)"
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- Article 13 creates no offence: the prohibition of 13(11)(a) carries no imprisonment and no fine.
-- src:401 | (11) A registered charity –
-- src:402 | (a) must not make any payment that is inconsistent with a statement provided under paragraph (9)(b);
@ref Article 13(11)(a) (src:401-402) -- the Law states no penalty
GIVETH A `Penalty provided`
`Art 13(11)(a) the penalty for a payment inconsistent with the statement` MEANS
    `Penalty provided` OF NOTHING, `no fine is provided`

-- src:403 | (b) may apply to the Commissioner, with reasons, for permission to amend that statement.
@ref Article 13(11)(b) (src:403)
@export The permission of a registered charity to apply to the Commissioner, with reasons, for permission to amend the statement of its current intentions as to payments, as a regulative rule: it applies once the charity has provided the statement
GIVEN `the entity is a registered charity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the entity is entered for the time being in the general or the restricted section of the register
      `a statement of intentions has been provided under Article 13(9)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the charity has provided the Commissioner with a statement of its current intentions
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Legal actor` `Act under Article 13`
`Art 13(11)(b) the registered charity may apply for permission to amend the statement` `the entity is a registered charity` `a statement of intentions has been provided under Article 13(9)(b)` MEANS
    IF     `the entity is a registered charity`
       AND `a statement of intentions has been provided under Article 13(9)(b)`
    THEN PARTY `a registered charity`
         MAY `apply to the Commissioner for permission to amend the statement of intentions` reasons
             PROVIDED NOT (reasons EQUALS "")
         HENCE FULFILLED
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- src:403 | (b) may apply to the Commissioner, with reasons, for permission to amend that statement.
@ref Article 13(11)(b) (src:403) -- the Commissioner's power to give permission is implied by these words
@export The Commissioner's permission (implied by Article 13(11)(b)) to grant a registered charity permission to amend the statement of its current intentions as to payments, as a regulative rule
GIVEN `someone is acting as the Commissioner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person appointed as the Commissioner, or a designated relevant person while the appointee cannot act, is acting
      `the charity has applied for permission to amend the statement, with reasons` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the registered charity has applied to the Commissioner, with reasons, for permission to amend the statement
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Legal actor` `Act under Article 13`
`Art 13(11)(b) the Commissioner may give permission to amend the statement` `someone is acting as the Commissioner` `the charity has applied for permission to amend the statement, with reasons` MEANS
    IF     `someone is acting as the Commissioner`
       AND `the charity has applied for permission to amend the statement, with reasons`
    THEN PARTY `the Commissioner`
         MAY `give an approval or permission` `permission to amend the statement of intentions as to payments, Article 13(11)(b)`
         HENCE FULFILLED
    ELSE FULFILLED

§§§ `13(13) Paragraphs (2) and (3) and an order of the court under the Loi of 1862`

-- The kinds of entity to which 13(13) speaks are the two that the Loi of 1862 governs: a court-approved fidéicommis (Article 2(1)(b)) and an
-- incorporated 1862 association (Article 2(1)(c)).  "To the extent that they are inconsistent": the Boolean answers it for one provision, so
-- a provision that is partly inconsistent is asked about once for each part.
-- src:405 | (13) If a court-approved fidéicommis or an incorporated 1862 association becomes registered as a charity under this Law, paragraphs (2) and (3) do not apply to that registered charity to the extent that they are inconsistent with any order made, whether before or after registration under this Law, by the court under the Loi of 1862.
@ref Article 13(13) (src:405)
@export Whether paragraphs (2) and (3) of Article 13 do not apply to a provision because an order of the court under the Loi of 1862 is inconsistent with them (a court-approved fideicommis or an incorporated 1862 association that has become a registered charity)
GIVEN `the registered charity` IS A `Registered charity` @desc What the register holds about the charity; its entity's kinds of entity say whether it is a court-approved fideicommis or an incorporated 1862 association
      provision IS A `Provision about amending purposes` @desc The provision, with the facts about any order of the court under the Loi of 1862
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 13(13) paragraphs (2) and (3) yield to an order under the Loi of 1862` `the registered charity` provision MEANS
        (   any (GIVEN kind YIELD kind EQUALS `the fidéicommissaires of a court-approved fidéicommis`)
                (`the registered charity`'s entity's `kinds of entity`)
         OR any (GIVEN kind YIELD kind EQUALS `an incorporated 1862 association`)
                (`the registered charity`'s entity's `kinds of entity`))
    AND provision's `an order of the court under the Loi of 1862 exists, made before or after registration`
    AND provision's `that order is inconsistent with paragraph (2) or (3) as applied to the provision`

§§§ `Integration point IP27 -- the Commissioner's decisions under Article 13`

-- Integration point IP27.  The Commissioner's decision on each, as a record of subject and outcome.  `domain.l4` has a subject for the first two;
-- the other two are "any other matter" (a nouns request: subjects for the permissions of 13(5)(b) and 13(11)(b)).
@ref Article 13(3)(b) (src:376), 13(4)(b) (src:379), 13(5)(b) (src:382), 13(11)(b) (src:403); Article 33(2)(d), (e) name the decisions
@export The Commissioner's decision on an approval or permission under Article 13, as a record of its subject and its outcome (integration point IP27, read by Article 33 for the right of appeal and by Schedule 1 paragraph 4(3) for the decisions staff may not take)
GIVEN about IS AN `Approval or permission of the Commissioner under Article 13` @desc Which approval or permission the decision is about
      `the Commissioner does what was sought` IS A BOOLEAN @desc TRUE if the Commissioner approves or permits what was sought; FALSE if the Commissioner refuses
GIVETH A `Decision of the Commissioner`
`Art 13 the decision of the Commissioner` about `the Commissioner does what was sought` MEANS
    `Decision of the Commissioner` WITH
        subject IS CONSIDER about
            WHEN `approval of a proposed amendment of the charity's purposes, Article 13(3)(b)`
                THEN `whether to approve a proposed amendment of the charity's purposes, Article 13(3)`
            WHEN `approval of a proposed amendment of the registered public benefit statement, Article 13(4)(b)`
                THEN `whether to approve a proposed amendment of the registered public benefit statement, Article 13(4)(b)`
            WHEN `prior permission to remain entered in the restricted section on the basis of a different condition, Article 13(5)(b)`
                THEN `any other matter`
            WHEN `permission to amend the statement of intentions as to payments, Article 13(11)(b)`
                THEN `any other matter`
        outcome IS IF `the Commissioner does what was sought`
                   THEN `the Commissioner does what was sought or proposed`
                   ELSE `the Commissioner refuses`
